From d86c23c22597e36da55fef83ba7d88d80386b95d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Garrett Brown <themagnificentmrb@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 00:03:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Synchronize the disc tray callback after loading a
 savestate

Savestates restore CD_TrayOpen but leave eject_state stale. Copy the
restored flag after a successful load so a later insert request cannot
open an already-closed tray.

MGS Debug-core regression:
- Before: both opposite-tray restores reported the old tray state.
- After: all four disc/no-disc and open/closed cases pass, including
  checks of the serialized internal state.
---
 libretro.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libretro.c b/libretro.c
index 58152217..c6449ed7 100644
--- a/libretro.c
+++ b/libretro.c
@@ -3923,6 +3923,8 @@ int StateAction(StateMem *sm, int load, int data_only)
    if(load)
    {
       ForceEventUpdates(0); // FIXME to work with debugger step mode.
+      if (ret)
+         eject_state = CD_TrayOpen;
    }
 
    return(ret);
